  <section>
    <h2>Management and privileged actions</h2>
    <p>Management is code-bound to loopback. The installed endpoint is normally <code>http://localhost:5080/</code>, and effective non-loopback overrides fail startup. There is no RC1 remote-management feature.</p>
    <p>The LocalSystem Windows service and the signed-in user's browser remain separate. The desktop opener reads a protected machine registry value, validates an HTTP loopback root endpoint, waits for <code>/health</code>, and opens the dashboard or Microsoft setup without elevation.</p>
    <p>Microsoft administration and printer Apply use fixed installed helpers with process, session, path, hash, and candidate checks. These controls reduce exposed functionality; they do not make a local Administrator untrusted.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Mail and identity boundaries</h2>
    <p>Device-to-RelayBridge SMTP is cleartext on one trusted private interface. Authenticated mode adds a device-specific credential, but that credential also crosses the private LAN without TLS. Legacy mode has no credential and therefore requires stricter private source isolation.</p>
    <p>RelayBridge-to-Exchange Online is a different connection. It requires normal certificate-validated STARTTLS on TCP 587 and XOAUTH2 using the customer-owned application and local certificate.</p>
    <p>Message content remains in the protected local spool while queued. An ambiguous upstream response can cause a retry and duplicate. A final Exchange <code>250</code> is acceptance by Microsoft at the SMTP boundary, not proof of inbox placement.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="rc1-limitations">
    <h2>RC1 limitations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Unsigned pre-release:</strong> Windows may show Unknown Publisher and SmartScreen may warn. RC1 is for evaluation and community testing, not the signed stable production release.</li>
      <li><strong>Windows client scope:</strong> Windows 10/11 x64 with one locally interactive administrator is supported. Windows Server, Server Core, RDP native setup, simultaneous setup users, x86, and Arm64 are not claimed.</li>
      <li><strong>No inbound STARTTLS:</strong> device SMTP, including reusable AUTH credentials, is cleartext on the trusted private LAN.</li>
      <li><strong>Manual firewall boundary:</strong> RelayBridge generates guidance but does not create or modify Windows Firewall rules.</li>
      <li><strong>One tenant, application, and sender:</strong> RC1 does not provide multi-tenant or multiple authorized-sender configuration.</li>
      <li><strong>Variable Exchange propagation:</strong> Step 5 checks are bounded; no duration is guaranteed and not every SMTP 535 is propagation.</li>
      <li><strong>No remote management:</strong> the management UI remains on local loopback.</li>
      <li><strong>No automatic updater:</strong> release checking is manual and informational; there is no automatic check, download, or installation.</li>
      <li><strong>No Graph delivery fallback:</strong> Exchange Online SMTP AUTH with OAuth/XOAUTH2 is the production delivery path.</li>
      <li><strong>At-least-once delivery:</strong> an ambiguous upstream failure can result in a retry and possible duplicate.</li>
      <li><strong>Acceptance is not inbox placement:</strong> Exchange <code>250</code> does not guarantee final delivery.</li>
      <li><strong>No automatic cleanup:</strong> uninstall preserves ProgramData and does not remove certificates, private keys, or Microsoft tenant objects.</li>
      <li><strong>No signed stable build:</strong> a signed stable RelayBridge v1.0.0 is not available.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Security reporting</h2>
    <p>Use the application's private vulnerability-reporting process described in <a href="https://github.com/getrelaybridge/relaybridge/blob/main/SECURITY.md">SECURITY.md</a>. Do not publish suspected vulnerabilities or include tenant identifiers, mailbox or message data, credentials, tokens, certificates, private keys, raw configuration, databases, spool files, or unreviewed support bundles in a public issue.</p>
